# City Gangster 3D

A small, playable browser-based prototype inspired by open-world city action games, but built from original code and assets only. This milestone focuses on a compact 3D city block with an on-foot character, a drivable car, mission checkpoint, HUD, and touch controls for mobile browser play.

## Included in this milestone

- Third-person character movement (walk, run, jump, rotation)
- Camera follow while on foot or in the car
- Small 3D city layout with roads, buildings, sidewalks, and streetlights
- One drivable car with steering, acceleration, braking, and collision handling
- Mission checkpoint and cash reward loop
- Traffic cars and pedestrians
- Mobile joystick and action buttons for Android browser play
- Desktop keyboard controls for testing on PC

## Requirements

- Node.js 18+
- Modern browser with WebGL support
- Android device on the same Wi‑Fi network for preview testing

## Install and run

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Then open the address printed by Vite, typically:

```text
http://localhost:4173
```

On your Android phone, open the same page using the PC's local IP address, for example:

```text
http://YOUR_PC_IP:4173
```

## Controls

### Desktop keyboard
- W / S / A / D: move
- Shift: run
- Space: jump
- E: enter or exit the vehicle

### Mobile touch
- Left joystick: walk or steer
- Jump button: jump
- Enter button: enter or exit vehicle

## Production export

This project is a browser-based prototype. To move it toward Android APK production, you would wrap the app with Android Studio WebView or port it into Unity. For Windows PC distribution, you would package the browser app into a desktop wrapper or port the gameplay to a native platform target.

## Important note

This project intentionally uses original code, original models, textures, and logic. It does not copy GTA trademarked content, maps, assets, music, proprietary code, or names.

## Project structure

- `src/main.ts` – bootstraps the application
- `src/game.ts` – city, player, car, mission, and controls
- `src/styles.css` – HUD and touch UI styling
- `index.html` – web app shell
- `vite.config.ts` – server configuration

## Build for production

```bash
npm run build
```

This will generate the `dist` folder for a static deployment or packaging pipeline.
